msgid "Description"
msgstr "Descrición"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: man-kded6.8.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kded6</command> consolidates several small services in one process. These are mostly &DBus; services provided by KDED modules, but it also manages sycoca (a binary cache of servicetypes, &MIME; types and services used by KService) and KConfig update scripts as needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kded5</command> consolidates several small services in one process. These are mostly &DBus; services provided by KDED modules, but it also manages sycoca (a binary cache of servicetypes, &MIME; types and services used by KService) and KConfig update scripts as needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: man-kded6.8.docbook:58
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "It monitors the directories containing .desktop files. When a file is added/removed, it waits 5 seconds (in case of a series of updates), and then launches <command>kbuildsycoca4</command> to update the sycoca."
msgid "For sycoca, it monitors the directories containing .desktop files. When a file is added/removed, it waits 5 seconds (in case of a series of updates), and then launches <command>kbuildsycoca6</command> to update the sycoca."
msgstr "Vixía os directorios que conteñen ficheiros .desktop. Cando se engade ou elimina un ficheiro agarda cinco segundos (por se é unha serie de actualizacións) e inicia <command>kbuildsycoca4</command> para actualizar o sycoca."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:58
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "It monitors the directories containing .desktop files. When a file is added/removed, it waits 5 seconds (in case of a series of updates), and then launches <command>kbuildsycoca4</command> to update the sycoca."
msgid "For sycoca, it monitors the directories containing .desktop files. When a file is added/removed, it waits 5 seconds (in case of a series of updates), and then launches <command>kbuildsycoca5</command> to update the sycoca."
msgstr "Vixía os directorios que conteñen ficheiros .desktop. Cando se engade ou elimina un ficheiro agarda cinco segundos (por se é unha serie de actualizacións) e inicia <command>kbuildsycoca4</command> para actualizar o sycoca."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6 trunk5
#: man-kded6.8.docbook:60
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "It checks newly installed update files, i.e. the *.upd files used to update configuration files of users when the configuration file formats changes. <command>kconf_update</command> is launched to do the updates."
msgid "For KConfig, it checks newly-installed update files, &ie; the *.upd files used to update configuration files of users when the configuration file formats changes, and runs the KConfig update utility to perform the updates."
msgstr "Comproba se hai instalados novos ficheiros de actualización, que son os ficheiros *.upd usados para actualizar os ficheiros de configuración dos usuarios cando hai modificacións no formato da configuración. <command>kconf_update</command>  iniciase para facer as actualizacións."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: man-kded6.8.docbook:62
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Those tasks are also performed always at kded4 start to ensure that the user configuration is up to date."
msgid "Those tasks are also run when <command>kded6</command> is started to ensure that the user configuration is up to date."
msgstr "Estas tarefas tamén se fan sempre no arranque de kded4 para garantir que a configuración do usuario estea ao día."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:62
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Those tasks are also performed always at kded4 start to ensure that the user configuration is up to date."
msgid "Those tasks are also run when <command>kded5</command> is started to ensure that the user configuration is up to date."
msgstr "Estas tarefas tamén se fan sempre no arranque de kded4 para garantir que a configuración do usuario estea ao día."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk6
#: man-kded6.8.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "You do not normally need to run <command>kded6</command> directly; &plasma; desktop sessions run it automatically, and it is started on demand when an application attempts to use a &DBus; interface provided by it or one of its modules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: man-kded5.8.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "You do not normally need to run <command>kded5</command> directly; &plasma; desktop sessions run it automatically, and it is started on demand when an application attempts to use a &DBus; interface provided by it or one of its modules."
msgstr ""

